From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:47:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(approval): a smart approval card's rule, reason,
 subagent and source are separate fields

The card of a smart approval was one run-on string ("Subagent "<goal>" asks: Smart approval rule "X": <reason>") and the reason could name internal call ids ("an earlier similar kill call (c56) was blocked") that nobody can look up.

The approval prompt event now carries `rule` (the rule name) and `reason` (the checker's words; a ledger write's entry and source lines follow as further lines) as fields of their own, next to `subagent` (the goal) and `grant_source`. `description` stays, with the same text as one string, for clients that do not read the fields. The review prompt asks the judge to name an earlier action by what it did, never by a transcript id, and the card strips any `c<digits>`, `call_...` or `toolu_...` reference that is left.
